/-!
# Concrete images of Parrott's generators

These ten permutations realize the generators on p. 683 of Parrott,
“A Characterization of the Tits’ Simple Group” (1972). They were discovered
by enumerating cosets of the subgroup generated by `s₁,…,s₈`, then finding
an isomorphism of the resulting permutation image with the ATLAS action.
This discovery procedure is not used as a proof: the inverse laws below,
and the relators and range certificates in `AtlasRepresentation`, are
checked by Lean's kernel against the concrete tables.

As in `AtlasPermutations`, the tables invert GAP's point maps and use
zero-based letters, preserving group-word multiplication.
-/

